schema.description:
Purpose: human-readable response preview on output.result for 2xx. SUCCESS shape EXACTLY: 'HTTP {METHOD} {url}
Status: {status}
Content-Type: {content_type}

Body:
{body_preview}'. {METHOD} is the allowlisted upper-case verb; {url} is the input URL; {status} is the numeric status; {content_type} is the Content-Type header lower-cased (empty if missing). Body: if the bytes parse as a JSON object or array they are re-serialized with Json.write (compact); otherwise raw text. Preview longer than 200000 characters is cut and suffixed with '... [truncated]'. The handler also caps the HTTP read at 200000 bytes (DoS bound). Example: 'HTTP GET https://httpbin.org/get
Status: 200
Content-Type: application/json

Body:
{"url":"https://httpbin.org/get"}'. No stack traces in this value.
